course: dictionary
lesson: 15863
title: Free and unfree
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unfree means not free. A person who is unfree is not allowed to choose how they live, work or move. «Long ago, serfs were unfree: they could not leave the land where they worked.» So a serf could not just go wherever they wanted.
explain: The word is built from two parts. Un- at the start means not, and free means able to choose. So unfree is the opposite of free. If you know free, you can work out unfree, and you can spot the same un- in words like unhappy and undo.
explain: Unfree can also describe a whole country or society. «The unfree country did not allow people to vote.» Here it means people there lack basic rights and freedoms. It is a formal word, so people often say «not free» instead.
fact: Unfree means not free.
fact: Un- at the start of a word means not, so unfree is the opposite of free.
fact: «Serfs» in medieval times were unfree; they could not leave the land they worked on.
fact: «Unfree» can describe a person, or a country where people lack rights and freedoms.
fact: It is a formal word, so in everyday talk you may say «not free» instead.
exercise: «The workers could not leave the farm, so they felt unfree.» What does unfree mean here? | Hungry after a long day | Free to travel anywhere they liked | *Not free to choose how they live or move | Very happy and calm
exercise: Which part of the word unfree means not? | The whole word together | The letter u on its own | *The un- at the start | The free at the end
exercise: «Serfs in medieval times were unfree.» Which word means the opposite of unfree? | medieval | times | serfs | *free
test: Which example shows a person who is unfree? | *A prisoner who cannot leave the prison | A bird flying over the hills | A family going on holiday | A child choosing what to eat for lunch
test: Which sentence uses unfree correctly? | Unfree the cat walked home. | The workers ate unfree sandwiches. | We went unfree to the park. | *The strict rules made the workers feel unfree.
exam: Which country would be called unfree? | A country where people can vote and speak freely | A country with many parks | A country with a long coastline | *A country where people cannot speak freely or vote
